Lichii PR #221 (zortos293/Lichii), second part only: while scanning a .pchtxt line for its
comment, a quote of the other kind inside a quoted string no longer toggles the quote state
(so "it's" or '"' no longer make a following // or # look like text). The first part, skipping
lines that are not patch records, is already done by headless/CMakeLists.txt (IsPatchRecord and
IsPatchFlag over Eden's IPSwitch parser), which replaces the code before Parse().

